  "findings": [
    "Home and detail Korean headings, leads, paragraphs and source sections are readable and fit each observed width. Narrow 320-pixel headings wrap over additional lines without observed truncation or horizontal overflow.",
    "Home uses the three approved banners separated by budget, facility and consultation content. The product-photo promise leads to the one real detail page; the home does not pretend to contain four product photos.",
    "Detail products are one column on mobile and two columns on desktop. B201, B203, B205 and B060 each show the correct distinct retained photograph, base price 59,000/79,000/109,000/149,000 KRW, separate shipping-total consultation label and SKU-specific CTA.",
    "The product-sample caveat is visible below the cards. Ribbon examples, total-budget distinction, Green facility address/telephone and conditional room/timing discussion follow the required products → ribbon → budget → facility → order sequence.",
    "All three FAQ questions and their complete answers are visible as open text in the full-page captures at all three widths, including cancellation-condition ambiguity, defect versus seasonal-material distinction, and paid-order unavailability.",
    "Support contains one real child card and no marketing banner. 404 and unknown-path captures provide a working-looking home recovery CTA and omit marketing banners. Their status and destinations are independently checked from retained report/HTML, not inferred from pixels.",
    "Mobile bottom home/telephone links are legible; primary body CTA heights are reported as at least44 pixels. Desktop nav and footer remain readable. The captures do not expose a fresh functional-blocking layout defect."
  ],
  "limits": [
    "This review inspects the original Actions loopback capture; no new interactive browser session was run by the reviewer.",
    "All 36 PNG files were opened. Six long full-page PNGs were read in 25 lossless contiguous native-scale segments, in addition to viewport/product/FAQ views; no pixels were altered or regenerated.",
    "Sticky header and fixed mobile action bars overlay parts of the tall element screenshots and mobile full-page captures. Product and FAQ content was cross-checked in unobscured full-page captures, alternate widths and exact DOM. This is not proof that every possible scroll/focus state is unobscured.",
    "Runner keyboard coverage is limited to first Tab/skip focus and mobile menu click, Space and Enter open/close, plus reported navigation/back/forward flows. No exhaustive Tab order, focus-visibility screenshots, screen reader or real-device testing was performed.",
    "No public live-browser, public HTTP, provider state, external checkout/call, stock, final delivery total, indexing or ranking result is established."
  ],
